Body:
Having a similar issue w/ bash commands.

## Expected

Commands set to `deny` in the opencode.jsonc file will be blocked by the permissions system.

## Actual

Any agent can run any command, whenever it pleases. There is no permissions filtering of any kind

## Evidence

```opencode.jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "synthetic/hf:zai-org/GLM-4.7",
  "share": "disabled",
  // Define permissions for model tooling
  "permission": {
    "question": "allow",
    "edit": "ask",
    "bash": {
      "pass-cli": "deny",
    },
    "webfetch": "allow",
    "doom_loop": "ask",
    "external_directory": "ask",
  },
  "agent": {
    "plan": {
      "model": "synthetic/hf:zai-org/GLM-4.7",
      "tools": {
        "read": true,
        "write": false,
        "edit": false,
        "bash": true,
      },
    },
    "build": {
      "model": "synthetic/hf:zai-org/GLM-4.7",
      "tools": {
        "read": true,
        "write": true,
        "edit": true,
        "bash": true,
      },
    },
  },
}
```

**Command is still run**
<img width="809" height="748" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38e129ca-b830-4f79-b5fb-7df47d3f42eb" />

##  Reproduce

Set any command to `deny` in the config, ask an agent to run said command.
